{"book":{"id":"book-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty","slug":"making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty","title":"Making Room: The Economics of Homelessness","authors":[{"id":"person-brendan-o-flaherty","name":"Brendan O'Flaherty"}],"publisherId":"publisher-harvard-university-press","imprintId":"imprint-harvard-university-press","isbn13":["9780674543430"],"subjects":["Business & Economics"],"topics":["Business, Capitalism & Corporations","Class, Poverty & Inequality","Housing, Cities & Urban Life","Money, Markets & Economic Policy"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Making%20Room%3A%20The%20Economics%20of%20Homelessness%20Brendan%20O'Flaherty","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Making%20Room%3A%20The%20Economics%20of%20Homelessness%20Brendan%20O'Flaherty","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Making%20Room%3A%20The%20Economics%20of%20Homelessness%20Brendan%20O'Flaherty","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Making%20Room%3A%20The%20Economics%20of%20Homelessness%20Brendan%20O'Flaherty","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL2962840W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-prose-economics-prose-awards-1996-winners-archive","source-cover-open-library-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty","source-imprint-normalization","source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"],"thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"academic","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0.454,"traits":[{"id":"academic","score":0.455,"confidence":"medium","evidence":["catalog text contains \"institutions\"","academic press signal: Harvard University Press / Harvard University Press"]},{"id":"scholarly","score":0.38,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"institutions\"","academic press signal: Harvard University Press / Harvard University Press"]},{"id":"argument_driven","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"theory\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Homelessness is best explained as a response to housing-market changes tied to widening rich-poor income gaps, shrinking the middle class, reducing low-income hand-me-downs, and raising rents.","confidence":0.63},"academicOrientation":{"score":55,"confidence":0.6},"profileConfidence":0.8,"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"d0e13a1811bd52139fd16f49554d8b898149524f51ca40b3b96ff7475aeee5ea","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Business & Economics","secondarySubjects":["Politics & Government","Society & Culture"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book primarily analyzes homelessness through an economic lens, focusing on market dynamics and their impact on housing, which aligns it most closely with Business & Economics, while also addressing related governmental and societal contexts.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"37707f0c197a3df83e75d8b99e7ee979c32ae7e95d838161acb54950fd38a4b7","summary":"Mentally ill people turned out of institutions, crack-cocaine use on the rise, more poverty, public housing a shambles: as attempts to explain homelessness multiply so do the homeless - and we still don't know why. The first full-scale economic analysis of homelessness, Making Room provides answers quite unlike those offered so far by sociologists and pundits. It is a story about markets, not about the bad habits or pathology of individuals. One perplexing fact is that, though homelessness in the past occurred during economic depressions, the current wave started in the 1980s, a time of relative prosperity. As Brendan O'Flaherty points out, this trend has been accompanied by others just as unexpected: rising rents for poor people and continued housing abandonment. These are among the many disconcerting facts that O'Flaherty collected and analyzed in order to account for the new homelessness. O'Flaherty shows that the conflicting observations begin to make sense when we see the new homelessness as a response to changes in the housing market, linked to a widening gap in the incomes of rich and poor. The resulting shrinkage in the size of the middle class has meant fewer hand-me-downs for the poor and higher rents for the low-quality housing that is available.","publicationYear":1996,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Housing","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Housing policy","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Homelessness","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Housing, canada","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Ill-Housed Persons","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Public Policy","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Homeless Persons","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Economics","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty"}],"displaySummary":"The first full-scale economic analysis of homelessness, Making Room provides answers quite unlike those offered so far by sociologists and pundits. It is a story about markets, not about the bad habits or pathology of individuals. One perplexing fact is that, though homelessness in the past occurred during economic depressions, the current wave started in the 1980s, a time of relative prosperity. As Brendan O'Flaherty points out, this trend has been accompanied by others just as unexpected: rising rents for poor people and continued housing abandonment. These are among the many disconcerting facts that O'Flaherty collected and analyzed in order to account for the new homelessness. O'Flaherty shows that the conflicting observations begin to make sense when we see the new homelessness as a response to changes in the housing market, linked to a widening gap in the incomes of rich and poor. The resulting shrinkage in the size of the middle class has meant fewer hand-me-downs for the poor and higher rents for the low-quality housing that is available.","primaryTopic":"Business, Capitalism & Corporations","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Business & Economics","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Business & Economics","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Business & Economics","mappedSubject":"Business & Economics","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily analyzes homelessness through an economic lens, focusing on market dynamics and their impact on housing, which aligns it most closely with Business & Economics, while also addressing related governmental and societal contexts.","id":"subject-evidence-book-making-room-the-economics-of-homelessness-brendan-o-flaherty-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject"